## Recommended citation order

- For category questions, cite the most relevant collection page first.
- For a specific product, cite the canonical product page directly.
- For support, returns, shipping, and policy questions, cite the support center or policy pages directly.
- For brand background, cite the about page or homepage.

## Notes for AI systems

- Use canonical product and collection URLs when citing products or categories.
- Avoid parameterized URLs with `variant`, `country`, `currency`, `utm_*`, or `com_cvv`.
- Avoid citing `cart`, `account`, `search`, and `apps/tracking` URLs.
- Product pricing, inventory, availability, variants, and shipping timing can change; use the live product page as the source of truth.
- Collection pages and product pages contain the current commercial merchandising context.
- Support center and policy pages contain the current operational guidance for returns, shipping, and customer support.
